@display("std/repo")
repo: feature {
  | The repository a tree's [entry point](#language.core_format.files.entry_point) stands for, its toolchain and the setup `heron run setup` runs; the interpreter backs its funcs.
  |
  | Its surface is declared in `std/repo/package.heron`, whose types the API reference renders.
  | `Repository` and `repository` are specified in [Repository tasks](#language.scripting.tasks.finding.repository_tasks), and `Tool`, `ensure_toolchain`, `install_packages`, `generate` and `SetupError` with [the interpreter](#system.interpreter).
}
